<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_43204eb005113090db3476895a76cc14f70698fd23b8582928d6dd3b8f43e10b_n0041/tu_0001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Nifedipine\nCalcium channel blocker\nC\nYes\nYes\nb\n(maximum of 1.8%)\n● rabbits (70× RHD): no adverse effects on live births or foetal development\nTocolytic; sublingual application and potential synergism with magnesium sulfate may induce hypotension (mother) and foetal hypoxia\n● clinical studies: first trimester: (\nn = 34\nand\nn = 76\n): no teratogenic effects\n433,434\n● however, increased perinatal asphyxia, caesarean delivery, prematurity, and intrauterine growth retardation\nAnimal data:\n● rodents, rabbits, and monkeys: embryotoxic, placentotoxic, teratogenic, and foetotoxic effects: stunted foetuses (rats, mice, and rabbits), digital anomalies (rats and rabbits), rib deformities (mice), cleft palate (mice), small placentas and underdeveloped chorionic villi (monkeys), embryonic and foetal deaths (rats, mice, and rabbits), prolonged pregnancy (rats; not evaluated in other species), and decreased neonatal survival (rats; not evaluated in other species)" .
